  "final_text": "Wrote `impact.txt` with 12 entries.\n\n**Method:** `who` on `src/attr/_make.py#_OBJ_SETATTR` returned 15 backlinks with `coverage.complete = true` (140 files across `src`, `tests`, `docs`, `bench`, `typing_tests`; `unresolved_matching: 0`), so nothing in the repo references it outside these. I dropped three of the 15:\n\n- `src/attr/_funcs.py` (module page, line 5) \u2014 just the `from ._make import _OBJ_SETATTR` line.\n- `src/attr/_make.py#_ClassBuilder` and `#Attribute` (class pages) \u2014 I read both class bodies; every use sits inside a method (or a closure nested in one), never at class-body level, so these are the class pages inheriting their methods' references.\n\n**Result:**\n\n```\nsrc/attr/_funcs.py#assoc\nsrc/attr/_funcs.py#resolve_types\nsrc/attr/_make.py#_transform_attrs\nsrc/attr/_make.py#_make_cached_property_getattr\nsrc/attr/_make.py#_ClassBuilder._patch_original_class\nsrc/attr/_make.py#_ClassBuilder._create_slots_class\nsrc/attr/_make.py#_ClassBuilder._make_getstate_setstate\nsrc/attr/_make.py#_ClassBuilder.add_setattr\nsrc/attr/_make.py#_make_init_script\nsrc/attr/_make.py#Attribute.__init__\nsrc/attr/_make.py#Attribute.evolve\nsrc/attr/_make.py#Attribute._setattrs\n```\n\nTwo notes on judgment calls:\n\n- No test file uses the name \u2014 the tests reference `object.__setattr__` directly, not the `_make` alias. The list is package-only despite the task anticipating test hits.\n- Four uses live in closures rather than in the named def itself: `slots_setstate` inside `_ClassBuilder._make_getstate_setstate`, and `__setattr__` inside `_ClassBuilder.add_setattr` (three uses there). Nested functions have no dotted form in the two shapes you specified, so I attributed each to its enclosing method. Renaming still has to touch those closure bodies.",
